<p>We are now in a position to provide several answers to those questions! First and foremost, let’s answer the questions that don't require much analysis. Yes, Codex can find interpretable heuristics - every time! Later on, we will spend some time analyzing those solutions. Importantly, we compared Codex 5.5 and xhigh settings, Claude Opus 4.7 in xhigh settings, and Gemini 3 pro. Overall, we find that Codex &gt; Claude &gt; Gemini. We present below the results, as well as the DRL results, for all cases:<sup class="sidenote-ref" data-note="15">15</sup><span class="sidenote" data-note="15" role="note"><span class="sidenote-number">15</span>We will release all markdown files and prompts very quickly!</span><span class="sidenote-mobile" data-note="15" role="note"><span class="sidenote-number">15</span>We will release all markdown files and prompts very quickly!</span></p>
